.SH NAME
messq-version - print build information


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmessq version [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Print the version, platform, Go toolchain and commit of this messq binary.

.PP
The default output follows the global --output contract: a human line
on a terminal, one JSON document otherwise. Add --remote to also ask
the daemon at --addr for its build and report any skew between the
two binaries.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for version

.PP
\fB--remote\fP[=false]
	also ask the daemon for its build (2 s budget)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB-a\fP, \fB--addr\fP="unix:///run/messq/messq.sock"
	daemon address (unix://, http://, https://)

.PP
\fB--color\fP="auto"
	colour: auto|always|never

.PP
\fB--full-ids\fP[=false]
	print full ULIDs instead of abbreviated ones

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP="auto"
	output mode: auto|table|json|ndjson

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	suppress narration; data and errors unaffected

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=30s
	per-request deadline (0 = none)

.PP
\fB--token-file\fP=""
	file holding the bearer token, mode 0600

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=0]
	narrate (-vv dumps each HTTP exchange and the resolved config)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  messq version
  messq version --output json | jq .commit
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBmessq(1)\fP


